## enterprise-linux audit baseline -- finalize (layer 13)
##
## "-e 2" makes the rule set immutable until reboot (STIG/CIS L2 expectation).
## It is OFF by default because:
##   * policy updates from eld/MDM could no longer change audit rules live;
##     every audit policy change would need a reboot;
##   * EDR agents that manage their own audit rules (some use auditd) break.
## Enable per policy once the update/reboot flow is in place.
#-e 2

## Make loginuid immutable once set. Off by default: breaks some container
## runtimes that need to set loginuid for their payloads.
#--loginuid-immutable
